{title: Low in the Grave He Lay (Christ Arose)}
{title_ko: 무덤에 머물러}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 160장}
{artist: Robert Lowry}
{genre: Easter}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: low-in-the-grave-he-lay.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Low in the grave He [C]lay, [G]Jesus my [D]Saviour
[G]Waiting the coming [C]day, [G]Jesus my [D]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Up from the grave He a[C]rose
With a [G]mighty triumph o'er His [D]foes
He a[G]rose a victor from the [C]dark do[G]main
And He [G]lives forever with His [C]saints to [D]reign
He a[G]rose! He a[C]rose! [G]Hallelu[D]jah! [G]Christ a[D]rose[G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Vainly they watch His [C]bed, [G]Jesus my [D]Saviour
[G]Vainly they seal the [C]dead, [G]Jesus my [D]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Death cannot keep his [C]prey, [G]Jesus my [D]Saviour
[G]He tore the bars a[C]way, [G]Jesus my [D]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
